{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1251\deff0\uc1{\fonttbl{\f0 Segoe UI;}}{\colortbl;\red28\green28\blue32;}\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs22 SEFI Launcher privacy policy\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Last updated: October 24, 2026.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 This policy describes the SEFI Launcher desktop application and the SEFI client mods shipped with it. The project is maintained by SEFI Team, with repository owner sotocoming (https://github.com/sotocoming) as the project contact. It describes the current implementation; it does not introduce new consent controls or change how an already installed release behaves.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 Automatic launcher updates\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Installed releases automatically check GitHub for new versions and download available updates in the background. A downloaded update can be installed when the launcher exits while no game is running. The interface also offers a manual check and an install/restart action. There is currently no separate setting to disable automatic update checks or downloads. These requests disclose connection information to GitHub and its download infrastructure.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 Connections and data\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b News, configuration, server status and map\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: SEFI services at mc.sotocoming.ru receive network request information such as IP address, time, requested resource and client headers. The map is loaded from that site. Remote news images can also contact their image hosts.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: Configuration and status are requested at startup and refreshed while the launcher runs. The map is loaded when opened.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b SEFI Community sign-in\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: The community service receives the browser sign-in exchange and issues a launcher session token. The launcher stores the community profile, including Minecraft name/UUID, Twitch login/avatar and access status. Saved community sessions are refreshed automatically. Twitch authentication takes place through the community website.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: When signing in, when a saved session is refreshed, and when checking access before game launch.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Microsoft / Xbox / Minecraft sign-in\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: Microsoft services receive authorization requests and issue tokens and the Minecraft name/UUID. When a community account is present, the launcher can send a Minecraft access token to the SEFI backend to verify and link that Minecraft profile; explicit linking also uses this verification. The Microsoft refresh token is not sent to the SEFI backend by this flow.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: When signing in, linking accounts or refreshing the Microsoft session needed to launch the game.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Skins and avatars\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: SEFI receives a selected skin PNG and model when you save it. Skin lookups use player names/UUIDs, including other players rendered by the SEFI skin mod. Avatar requests to mc-heads.net include a player name or UUID. Twitch avatar URLs may contact Twitch image hosts. Those hosts also see network request information.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: When displaying an avatar, loading a saved skin, saving/resetting a skin, or rendering community players in Minecraft.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Game and Java downloads\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: Minecraft/Microsoft, Fabric, CurseForge, Modrinth, Eclipse Adoptium, GitHub, their download/CDN hosts and the SEFI download mirror receive download requests and connection information. Authenticated SEFI mirror requests include the community token; it is not forwarded to external download hosts.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: When installing, repairing or launching a game that needs files, or preparing the managed Java runtime.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Launcher updates\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: GitHub and its download infrastructure receive requests for release metadata and update files, with connection information and updater headers.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: Installed releases check automatically and download available updates in the background.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Discord activity\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: The launcher sends game/launcher state, play start time, game dimension, player count and the configured server-region label to the local Discord application. Discord can publish that activity according to the user's Discord settings. The launcher also requests the Discord application's icon metadata and uses a Discord CDN image URL.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: Enabled by default; can be disabled in launcher settings.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b Interface fonts\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Data and recipients: Google Fonts receives font/style requests and connection information from the interface.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 When: When the interface loads and the font is fetched.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 These connections support the features above. Closing the launcher stops its background work, but does not close a game or browser already opened from it. The game and third-party mods may make their own connections and are subject to their respective policies.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 Reports and optional input diagnostics\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 A launch or crash report can also be prepared manually in the launcher. Opening the form does not upload anything. The user chooses attachments: launcher version, OS, architecture and allocated memory; a limited launch log; game warnings and errors; or a crash file from the last launch. The launcher keeps bounded current-launch records in memory and checks only known log and crash files for that launch when preparing a report. After restarting the launcher, saved errors and crashes from the last 24 hours can be selected manually; they are labeled as a previous session and are unchecked by default. Known authentication data, personal paths and recognized chat lines are filtered before preview. The preview shows the prepared contents; the comment and Discord-ticket option are also chosen by the user.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Launcher reports go directly to the authenticated SEFI endpoint only when the user presses Send to website. A manual retry of the same contents keeps the same report ID. There are no automatic uploads or background retries. Without signing in, a JSON copy can be saved to a folder chosen through Save a copy. The website stores reports for SEFI support. If a ticket is requested, Discord receives the description and a diagnostic link accessible to panel administrators.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 The in-game /report form sends data only after the user chooses to send a report. It includes the entered title, description and reproduction steps, plus selected attachments. Available attachments include mod names, versions and hashes, Java/OS and graphics information, resource-pack information, selected settings and key bindings, limited gameplay context, and filtered warning/error lines. Attachments are selected by default but can be excluded and previewed. The form also offers saving a local copy without sending it.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Input recording starts only when the user enables it, lasts up to two minutes, and records mouse-button/modifier and game-input state rather than typed chat. A recording is attached only if it exists and the input attachment is selected. Filtering is not a guarantee that every possible personal detail is removed: review the preview and do not enter passwords or other secrets in free text.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 In-game /report submissions pass through a service bound to 127.0.0.1 on the user's computer and then to the authenticated SEFI report endpoint. A local copy is saved in sefi-reports inside the game directory. The Discord-ticket option is selected by default and can be disabled before sending; if enabled, the server can forward report data to a Discord support ticket. Reports are for the SEFI support team, and linked Discord authors may be given access to their ticket. Server availability and account linking determine whether a ticket can be created.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 Local storage and removal\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 The launcher stores settings, cached configuration, account identifiers and session credentials under its Electron user-data directory (normally the sefi-launcher folder inside %APPDATA% on Windows). It maintains accounts.json and a recovery copy, accounts.json.bak. The Microsoft refresh token is encrypted with Electron safeStorage (Windows DPAPI). This does not mean all stored account fields or all other tokens are encrypted; protect access to the Windows profile.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Removing an account updates the active account file. It does not revoke provider permissions, delete the SEFI website account or necessarily remove that account from the recovery copy. To remove all local launcher credentials, close the launcher and remove its account file and recovery copy, or its user-data folder. Removing the folder also removes launcher settings. Revoke external access separately through the relevant provider when needed.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Game files, settings backups, local reports and input recordings are stored in the selected game directory. The managed Java runtime is kept in the launcher user-data directory. Uninstalling the application preserves application data; it does not automatically delete these files. Delete unneeded files yourself when the launcher and Minecraft are closed, preserving any worlds or settings you want to keep.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 Control, server storage and contact\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 You can disable Discord activity in settings, omit report attachments, disable Discord-ticket creation, save reports locally, and choose not to start an input recording. Removing a saved account stops the launcher's use of that account except for copies you retain. The current release has no single offline/privacy switch: automatic update, configuration, status, font and avatar requests are not all controlled by separate switches.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Removing local files does not delete profiles, uploaded skins, reactions, submitted reports, support tickets, server logs or backups already held by SEFI or an external provider. The client does not set a universal deletion deadline for those server-side records. For access, correction, retention or deletion questions, contact the administrator at sotocoming@proton.me. Do not include passwords, access tokens or other credentials in your message. If identification is needed to handle your request, the administrator will explain which information is required.\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \b\fs20 External service policies\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 External providers operate their own services and infrastructure:\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Microsoft, Xbox and Minecraft privacy statement (https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Twitch privacy notice (https://legal.twitch.com/en/legal/privacy-notice/)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Discord privacy policy (https://discord.com/privacy)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? GitHub privacy statement (https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Google privacy policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Eclipse Foundation / Adoptium privacy policy (https://www.eclipse.org/legal/privacy/)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Modrinth privacy policy (https://modrinth.com/legal/privacy)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? MCHeads service information (https://mc-heads.net/) (avatar lookup provider)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? Fabric service information (https://fabricmc.net/) (loader and library metadata/downloads)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 \u8226? CurseForge (https://www.curseforge.com/) (modpack and mod downloads; see its current privacy links)\par
\pard\plain\li0\fi0\sa100\sl240\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 Changes to the launcher's data handling should be reflected in this document with a new revision date. Consult the policy for the version you use.\par}
